# 🟡 Level 2 – HTTP & HTTPS

# What is HTTP?

HTTP = **HyperText Transfer Protocol**

Used for communication between:

Browser

↓

Web Server

Example

```text
GET /index.html
```

Server replies

```text
200 OK
```

---

# HTTPS

HTTPS = HTTP + TLS Encryption

Benefits

✔ Encryption

✔ Integrity

✔ Authentication

---

# HTTP Request

Example

```http
GET /login HTTP/1.1

Host: example.com
```

Contains:

* Method
* URL
* Headers
* Body (if applicable)

---

# HTTP Response

Example

```http
HTTP/1.1 200 OK

Content-Type: text/html
```

Contains:

* Status Code
* Headers
* Content

---

# HTTP Methods

## GET

Retrieve information.

Example:

```text
View Products
```

---

## POST

Send data.

Example:

```text
Login Form

Registration
```

---

## PUT

Update an existing resource.

---

## DELETE

Delete a resource.

---

## PATCH

Partially update a resource.

---

# Common HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Meaning                                          |
| ---- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| 200  | Success                                          |
| 201  | Resource Created                                 |
| 301  | Permanent Redirect                               |
| 302  | Temporary Redirect                               |
| 400  | Bad Request                                      |
| 401  | Unauthorized (authentication required or failed) |
| 403  | Forbidden (authenticated but not permitted)      |
| 404  | Not Found                                        |
| 500  | Internal Server Error                            |
| 503  | Service Unavailable                              |

