# 🟠 Level 3 – Cookies & Sessions

# Cookies

A cookie is a small piece of data stored by the browser.

Example:

```text
Username

Theme

Language

Session ID
```

---

# Why Cookies?

Without cookies,

every page would behave like a brand-new visitor.

You would need to log in repeatedly.

---

# Sessions

A Session stores user information on the **server**.

Example

```text
Login

↓

Server Creates Session

↓

Session ID

↓

Browser Cookie

↓

Future Requests
```

---

# Cookie vs Session

| Cookie                   | Session                                  |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| Stored in browser        | Stored on server                         |
| Small amount of data     | User state stored securely on server     |
| May include a session ID | Uses the session ID to identify the user |

---

# Authentication vs Authorization

## Authentication

Question:

> Who are you?

Example:

Username

Password

MFA

---

## Authorization

Question:

> What can you do?

Example:

Admin

↓

Delete User

Employee

↓

View Own Profile

---

# 🌍 Real-World Example

You log into Gmail.

Authentication:

✔ Username

✔ Password

✔ OTP

Authorization:

✔ Read Email

✔ Send Email

✔ Delete Own Email

❌ Cannot read another user's mailbox.

